<h2>Login (Insecure)</h2>

<p>
  This login form is intentionally vulnerable to SQL injection.
  On the backend I build the SQL query by concatenating the email and password
  directly into the SQL string.
</p>

<p>Seeded Test Account:</p>
<pre>
Email: conor@test.com
Password: Pass123
</pre>

<% if (error) { %>
  <!-- I show a simple error message here if the login fails -->
  <p style="color:red;"><%= error %></p>
<% } %>

<form method="post" action="/login">
  <label>Email</label><br>
  <input name="email" type="text"><br><br>

  <label>Password</label><br>
  <input name="password" type="password"><br><br>

  <button type="submit">Login</button>
</form>

<hr>

<h3>SQL Injection Demo</h3>
<p>Example payload to test the vulnerability in the email field:</p>
<code>' OR 1=1 --</code>